'' A COPY CONSTRUCTOR WITH A DEFAULTED SECOND PARAMETER. An initialiser and a 'return' resolve
'' the overload and run it; a byval argument does not, because fbc's copy-constructor fact
'' counts only a one-parameter one, so the type stays trivial. Expected output is fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/copyctor-defaulted.bas -o tests/codegen/copyctordefaulted.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/copyctordefaulted.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [init][conv][ret][copy][copy] g: 205
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [conv][ret][copy] h: 105
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [conv][copy] k: 107
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [conv]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  in: 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [copy] b: 101
